{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>יגונב</b> — from גנב, its meaning: it is snatched away." "<b>שמץ מנהו</b> — all the commentators explained it as 'a little,' according to context. But the correct interpretation in my eyes: it is from the sense of ומה שמץ דבר נשמע בו (1 Kings 19:12), and its meaning: that my ear cannot grasp the fine, excellent thing from it, like the matter of 'face and back' mentioned in the pericope of כי תשא."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:16.990336222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}